order/createStorepickupCode/{idEcommerce}/{idOrder} differs from LAN in its contract:
- verb: [HttpGet] here, POST in LAN;
- success body: a JSON string with estado and clave (StorePickupMethods.cs:446) instead of 'ok';
- errors: 500 InternalServerError(e) instead of 400 BadRequest.

MVC template leftovers in a Web API project:
- appSettings webpages:Version, webpages:Enabled, ClientValidationEnabled and UnobtrusiveJavaScriptEnabled;
- Global.asax.cs calls AreaRegistration.RegisterAllAreas() and imports System.Web.Mvc and System.Web.Optimization, but there are no Areas, Views or bundles.

The csproj and packages carry unused MVC/SPA template dependencies and folders:
- references System.Web.Mvc, Razor, WebPages(.Deployment/.Razor), Helpers, Optimization, WebGrease and Antlr3;
- packages.config has bootstrap, jQuery, Modernizr, Mvc, Razor, Optimization, WebGrease, Antlr and WebApi.HelpPage;
- Folder entries App_Data, Views\BusinessPartner, Views\Order and Views\Sale, and WCFMetadata 'Connected Services', none of which exist on disk.

Microsoft Fakes leftovers, which the user has stated are obsolete and were generated by accident:
- a Reference to Conexion.1.0.0.0.Fakes with its HintPath in FakesAssemblies\;
- a Reference to Microsoft.QualityTools.Testing.Fakes v12;
- Fakes items Fakes\ConexionSap.fakes and Fakes\Conexion.fakes.
